  "verbalization": "Cryptobeilic Acid C appears to interact with Isopentenyl-diphosphate Delta-isomerase through a multi-step pathway, with the target enzyme being PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. This suggests that Cryptobeilic Acid C may act as a modulator of the kinase activity of CDC2L1, which in turn influences the activity of Isopentenyl-diphosphate Delta-isomerase. The evidence indicates that Cryptobeilic Acid C targets CDC2L1, which is a known target of (-)-Valeranone, further suggesting a potential metabolic or signaling cascade involving these compounds. The integration of these pathways implies that Cryptobeilic Acid C may exert its effects by regulating the activity of CDC2L1, which then affects the activity of Isopentenyl-diphosphate Delta-isomerase. This mechanism highlights a possible role for Cryptobeilic Acid C in modulating isopentenyl-diphosphate metabolism, potentially through the regulation of kinase activity in the pathway.",
